      "name": "A0/D0",
      "label": "A0/D0 (GPIO0)",
      "codeName": "D0",
      "capabilities": [
        "analog_input",
        "digital_input",
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output"
      ],
      "notes": "BAT_MEASURE/MSR/BAT_VOLT_PIN in this board's pins_arduino.h. Optional onboard battery-voltage sense: a 200k:200k resistor divider (1:2 ratio) is connected ahead of this pin ONLY when the \"MSR\" solder pads on the back of the board are bridged - normally this pin is a plain general-purpose analog/digital GPIO. If MSR is bridged, battery voltage = analogRead(A0)/4095 * 3.3V * 2 (approx - PCB Cupid's own forum notes real-world ESP32 ADC nonlinearity may need an empirical calibration factor around 1.1-1.15x). Confirmed via learn.pcbcupid.com Power Management/Pinouts docs and forum.pcbcupid.com \"Glyph C6 Battery Measurement issue\" thread."
    },
